Cell["\<\
What counts as equal is \"CanonicalizeStates\". By default it is up to \
canonical form, so two states differing only in what their vertices are \
called are one. Comparing them as written merges far less:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"842f144f-31ff-1843-b3ad-f6a9fb9d2c49"],

Cell["\<\
{VertexCount @ twoEdges[\"StatesGraph\", 2, \"StateRendering\" -> False],
  VertexCount @ twoEdges[\"StatesGraph\", 2, \"CanonicalizeStates\" -> False,
     \"StateRendering\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5b045bda-5229-b64f-a7aa-1bb047f43467"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"8", ",", "9"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d698b034-04e1-6d49-afcc-33a83992908e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "A rewrite names the vertices it creates after what is already there, so two \
branches that reach the same shape rarely reach it under the same names. \
Without canonicalizing, a states graph of a growing rule barely merges \
anything and is just the tree again."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"6a02e1b1-b5e6-de42-bc80-b826f32b0374"],

Cell["BranchialGraph \[LongDash] what one step could have done", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6ffa4ae8-c676-0545-9d80-fcb6372466d5"],

Cell["\<\
The states of a single generation, joined when they came from the same state:\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd9b2673-c8a8-9041-99e7-5071b5e286e3"],

Cell["\<\
twoEdges[\"BranchialGraph\", 1, ImageSize -> 400, \"PanelSize\" -> 90]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a7e1522d-0c44-7643-a876-a47938fe1e79"],

